.	http://www.emsl.pnl.gov/ecce:annotation		xTB, GFN-FF, single point of a polyalanine alpha-helix. This calculation shows a helix with 3.6 residues per turn and a rise of 1.5 A per residue, which gives a fibre pattern with a strong reflection at 1.5 A on the meridian and a layer line at the pitch of 5.4 A.
